    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Three states, never two",
      "items": [
        "library: — the name is explained by a dynamic library that is present",
        "gpu_kernel: — the name is a CUDA / AMD kernel found inside the binary",
        "missing: — no evidence was found; the tool says so instead of guessing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Only explicit binaries count",
      "items": [
        "Attribution uses exactly the files passed on the command line",
        "Anything not supplied stays missing — a false positive is worse than no attribution",
        "The engine walks the container first, then its dependency list, symbol table and GPU sections"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Where the GPU names come from",
      "items": [
        "CUDA fatbin to cubin: the kernel name sits in the .text._Z section-name table",
        "AMD HSA code object and Vulkan SPIR-V entry points are read the same way",
        "A cubin is not a standard ELF: e_type 0x8000 and e_shoff 0xCAFE are sentinels"
      ]
    }
